            <ArticleTitle>The utilization of electronic patient record in pain management from the perspective of nursing management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>171-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">The electronic patient record is becoming more common in Finland. Structured and classified documentation methods make it possible to utilize different reports from EPR in the nursing management.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe how the knowledge of pain management in the EPR can be utilized in nursing management.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The descriptive data were collected from electronic patient records of patients with joint replacement in May 2008.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There were 30 notes in the intensity measurement/assessments of pain versus 1788 in the pain control.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The patient records show shortage in nursing documentation. This paper does not show the reason and therefore further research is needed. However this makes the nursing manager act.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
